What was derived, specifically: the parser architecture in
`src/mfc_api/parsers/` — a parser class per page, given HTML, returning a
model.

The CSS selectors are not derived. MFC's templates moved on since tenji's
last release, and every selector here was written against pages captured in
2026. Two endpoints tenji used are gone entirely (`itemlists.v4.php` now
404s), and the collection, profile, list and shop pages all render different
markup than it expects.

One piece of tenji does survive verbatim: the Buy window is a form POST to
`/item/{id}` with `commit=loadWindow&window=buyItem`, answering with JSON.
That request envelope is tenji's discovery and it still works in 2026.

See the Credits section of README.md for the fuller account.
